("Node's `fetch` needs absolute URLs; jsdom doesn't provide a `fetch`. Fix by using an absolute `API_URL` in tests (environment variable) or by installing a fetch wrapper that resolves relative to `location`. Don't paper over by prefixing in only some call sites. ⚠ Verify current behavior for your Vitest/jsdom versions; some setups polyfill differently.",
 "Node's `fetch` needs absolute URLs; jsdom doesn't provide a `fetch`, so in a jsdom Vitest run `fetch` is Node's. Verified: relative URLs fail with `TypeError: Failed to parse URL from /api/x` whenever MSW is not intercepting (no `server.listen()`, a `node` environment, or code that runs before `listen()`); with MSW listening under jsdom they are resolved against `location`. Fix by using an absolute `API_URL` in tests (environment variable) or by installing a fetch wrapper that resolves relative to `location`. Don't paper over by prefixing in only some call sites."),
("Remedies: use `happy-dom` (⚠ verify its behavior), or delete the jsdom globals so Node's are used (a setup-file override such as re-assigning `globalThis.AbortController`/`AbortSignal` from Node's); verify against the Vitest and MSW issue trackers/docs for your versions. This is environment plumbing; keep the workaround in one clearly commented setup file.",
 "*Reproduced on Vitest 3.2.7 + jsdom 30 + Node 24 + MSW 2.15.0:* `fetch(url, { signal: new AbortController().signal })` throws `TypeError: RequestInit: Expected signal (\"AbortSignal {}\") to be an instance of AbortSignal`. `happy-dom` showed the **same** error in the same setup, so it is not a remedy. Verified remedy: run tests that exercise cancellable `fetch` in the Node environment with a per-file docblock `// @vitest-environment node` (there, `AbortController` aborts cleanly with `AbortError`). For jsdom component tests, inject the fetching function or avoid passing a signal in those tests; re-check upstream (Vitest/jsdom/undici issue trackers) before inventing a global override. This is environment plumbing; keep any workaround in one clearly commented place."),
